        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agent-core): avoid a crash when empty output has a negative line limit",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where developers using the agent-core truncation helper would see a crash when empty output is evaluated with a negative line limit.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe head-truncation path now handles empty input before calculating first-line bytes and returns the existing structured truncation result. Valid non-empty truncation behavior is unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgent-core consumers now receive truncation metadata instead of an exception for this empty-output boundary case.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: `truncateHead` no longer throws for empty output with negative line or byte ceilings when called through OpenClaw's session-tool truncation facade.\n- Head: `8ed74057b1253f2740186d334bd7ac82299b947f`\n- Commands / artifacts:\n  - `node --import tsx --input-type=module -` importing `truncateHead` from `src/agents/sessions/tools/truncate.ts`\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/agent-core/src/harness/utils/truncate.test.ts` (9 passed)\n  - `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`\n  - GitHub CI for this head is passing, including `build-artifacts`, `check-lint`, `check-test-types`, and compact Node shards.\n- Observed runtime result:\n\n```text\nhead=8ed74057b1253f2740186d334bd7ac82299b947f\nempty + negative maxLines\n{\n  \"content\": \"\",\n  \"truncated\": true,\n  \"truncatedBy\": \"lines\",\n  \"totalLines\": 0,\n  \"totalBytes\": 0,\n  \"outputLines\": 0,\n  \"outputBytes\": 0,\n  \"firstLineExceedsLimit\": false\n}\nempty + negative maxBytes\n{\n  \"content\": \"\",\n  \"truncated\": true,\n  \"truncatedBy\": \"bytes\",\n  \"totalLines\": 0,\n  \"totalBytes\": 0,\n  \"outputLines\": 0,\n  \"outputBytes\": 0,\n  \"firstLineExceedsLimit\": false\n}\n```",
        "branch": "codex/fix-truncate-head-empty-limit",
